{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3154","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3154","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3154\",\"parent_revision\":\"71a5c4ba9c57f9f0777940caf09790b1f31060bd\",\"root_revision\":\"027d805b89507c0ac0bdc19deaf4985c455242479f7d5e10641082ece05469fc\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-22\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAn item's `groomed` metadata field and its `status:*` label can disagree about whether the item has been groomed.\\n\\nObserved on #3151 and reproduced on #3152. Reading #3152 during its fix on 2026-08-23:\\n\\n    \\\"labels\\\": [\\\"priority:p1\\\", \\\"type:bug\\\", \\\"status:needs-grooming\\\"],\\n    \\\"groomed\\\": \\\"2026-08-22\\\",\\n    \\\"status\\\": \\\"needs-grooming\\\"\\n\\nThe date field says the item was groomed on 2026-08-22. The label says it still needs grooming.\\n\\nApparent mechanism, to be confirmed during grooming: `backlog_groom` takes a `mark_groomed` parameter that defaults to `False`. Its documented effect when `True` is to \\\"advance item status to groomed after content is written: set local frontmatter status to 'groomed', remove status:needs-grooming label (idempotent), and add status:groomed label.\\\" A `backlog_groom` call made without `mark_groomed=True` therefore writes content and \u2014 on the evidence above \u2014 stamps a groom date, without moving the status label. Whether the date stamp is written by `backlog_groom` itself or by something else in the write path has not been traced.\\n\\nWhy this matters rather than being cosmetic: consumers disagree depending on which field they read. `work/prepare.md` Step 3.1 branches on the date field \u2014 \\\"**Ungroomed** (`groomed` absent or empty): run the grooming workflow\\\" versus \\\"**Groomed** (`groomed` = date string): run two-phase staleness check before consuming cached content.\\\" An item in this state takes the groomed branch and has its (possibly absent) groomed content treated as cached and merely stale, while any consumer filtering on `status:needs-grooming` still sees it as untouched. The work workflow and the label-based views can each be internally consistent and still reach opposite conclusions about the same item.\\n\\nGrooming should settle which of the two is the source of truth, and whether the fix is to stop stamping the date unless `mark_groomed=True`, to make the two always move together, or to have consumers read one canonical signal.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **items carry a groomed date while still labelled status:needs-grooming, so the two disagree about whether grooming happened** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 2026-08-23, split out of #3152 during its fix\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-22\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"af9f2fdfe1fd01ae7e9ec2fff8b4d3b6486da642ee585e523bb4c4aad85cf7ef\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABQOID0w\"}"}